# Individual: <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00010344> (CRF sector (IPCC 2006): ammonia production)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00010344> "The CRF sector (IPCC 2006) 'ammonia' is an industry sector defined by the 2006 IPCC Guidelines for National Greenhouse Gas Inventories:
Ammonia (NH3) is a major industrial chemical and the most important nitrogenous material produced. Ammonia gas is used directly as a fertilizer, in heat treating, paper pulping, nitric acid and nitrates manufacture, nitric acid ester and nitro compound manufacture, explosives of various types, and as a refrigerant. Amines, amides, and miscellaneous other organic compounds, such as urea, are made from ammonia. The main greenhouse gas emitted from NH3 production is CO2. CO2 used in the production of urea, a downstream process, should be subtracted from the CO2 generated and accounted for in the AFOLU Sector.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00010344> "2006 IPCC Guidelines for National Greenhouse Gas Inventories, Volume 1, Chapter 8.5, https://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp/public/2006gl/")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00010344> "CRF sector (IPCC 2006): ammonia production"@en)
